/* Learning Data: In the weeds of data crafting. The words of the series' labs (Take it apart) and scenarios (Make the call), in
   English. Keep the keys in step with learn.es.js. One playground for each film, each on the chapter it plays (film, chapter), with
   three to five experiments (w.goals) the visitor ticks by making them happen; and twelve situations from every film, the series'
   evaluation, each pointing to its playground. learn.js draws every picture from these words and keeps progress in this browser under
   "ld-in-the-weeds": the labs visited, the experiments ticked, and the answers by scenario number (film × 10 + its place, from 2, so an
   answer kept from the series' earlier situations, numbered film × 10 + 1, is never read as one of these).
   A page shows each situation's options in the order written here: the right answers are spread across the places, and the Spanish
   pack keeps them in the same places.
   build_series.py (series_learn) reads the first keys of each lab, in this order: id, kind, film, chapter, c, name; and of each
   scenario: type, n, lab, film. No other object here starts with id, and no other key is called kind or starts an object with type.
   Names and numbers follow the films' narration: Jun, Noor, Mei in the registrar's office, Aisha and her three keys, Priya's late
   withdrawal, the census report's twelve, Health's renamed certificate, Finance's 67,800 dollars. */
